# Markdown Frontmatter for docs/

Every new `.md` file created inside `docs/` must start with YAML frontmatter following the Harle vault convention defined in `docs/trd/architecture/data.md`.

## Required format

```yaml
---
title: "Descriptive title with key terms"
tags: [lowercase, hyphenated-multi-word, tags]
context: global
last_updated: YYYY-MM-DD
summary: "One-sentence description of what this document covers."
---
```

## Field rules

- **title** — matches the document's H1 heading or describes its content.
- **tags** — 3–7 lowercase, hyphenated tags. Include at least one domain tag and one action/type tag. Use the existing tag vocabulary in the project when possible.
- **context** — use `global` for project documentation in `docs/`.
- **last_updated** — set to the current date when creating or modifying the file.
- **summary** — a single sentence describing the document's purpose. Keep it under 200 characters.

## Tag style

- Lowercase only, hyphenate multi-word tags: `data-layer`, not `DataLayer`.
- Prefer specific terms over generic ones: `postgresql` over `database`.

## Example

```markdown
---
title: "Harle Orchestrator — Architecture & Functionality"
tags: [orchestrator, architecture, fastapi, agents, routing, context-assembly, tools]
context: global
last_updated: 2026-02-19
summary: "Describes the Orchestrator's internal modules, request lifecycle, conversation mode, and technology choices."
---

# Harle Orchestrator — Architecture & Functionality

> The Orchestrator is the central component of Harle...
```
